Active site","start":360,"end":360,"description":""},{"type":"Site","start":374,"end":375,"description":"Cleavage; by CASP6"},{"type":"Propeptide","start":375,"end":384,"description":""},{"type":"Modified residue","start":380,"end":380,"description":"Phosphotyrosine; by SRC"},{"type":"Site","start":384,"end":385,"description":"Cleavage; by autocatalytic cleavage"},{"type":"Chain","start":385,"end":479,"description":"Caspase-8 subunit p10"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":387,"end":387,"description":"Phosphoserine; by CDK1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":413,"end":413,"description":"(Microbial infection) ADP-riboxanated arginine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterotetramer that consists of two anti-parallel arranged heterodimers, each one formed by a 18 kDa (p18) and a 10 kDa (p10) subunit (PubMed:10508784). Component of the death-induced signaling complex (DISC) composed of cell surface receptor FAS/CD95 or TNFRSF1A, adapter protein FADD and the CASP8 protease; recruitment of CASP8 to the complex is required for processing of CASP8 into the p18 and p10 subunits (PubMed:8681376, PubMed:8681377, PubMed:9184224). Component of complex IIa at least composed of RIPK1, FADD and CASP8 (PubMed:12887920, PubMed:18485876). Component of the AIM2 PANoptosome complex, a multiprotein complex that drives inflammatory cell death (PANoptosis) (By similarity). Interacts with PEA15 (PubMed:10442631). Interacts with TIPE2 (By similarity). Interacts with CASP8AP2 (PubMed:16378960). Interacts with RFFL and RNF34; negatively regulate CASP8 through proteasomal degradation (PubMed:15069192). Interacts with NOL3; decreases CASP8 activity in a mitochondria localization- and phosphorylation-dependent manner and this interaction is dissociated by calcium (PubMed:15509781). Interacts with UBR2ca (PubMed:28602583). Interacts with stimulated TNFRSF10B; this interaction is followed by CASP8 proteolytic cleavage and activation (PubMed:18846110). Interacts (phosphorylated on Tyr-380) with PIK3R1 (PubMed:27109099). Interacts with long isoform of CFLAR (FLIP-L, also named isoform 1); promoting CASP8 enzymatic activity toward RIPK1, leading to RIPK1 cleavage and inactivation, thereby preventing necroptosis (PubMed:21737329)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with human cytomegalovirus/HHV-5 protein vICA/UL36; this interaction inhibits CASP8 activation"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with NleF from pathogenic E.coli"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with molluscum contagiosum virus protein MC160"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts (via RIP homotypic interaction motif) with herpes simplex virus 1/HHV-1 protein RIR1/ICP6 (via RIP homotypic interaction motif); this interaction prevents necroptosis activation"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts (via RIP homotypic interaction motif) with herpes simplex virus 2/HHV-2 protein RIR1/ICP10 (via RIP homotypic interaction motif); this interaction prevents necroptosis activation"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q14790-2","name":"2","synonyms":["Alpha-2","MCH5-beta"],"notes":[],"length":464,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000323492.11","ENST00000392263.6","ENST00000696087.1"],"refseq":["NM_001080124.2","NM_001400658.1","NM_001400659.1","NM_001400660.1","NM_001400661.1","NM_001400662.1","NM_001400663.1","NM_033356.4"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001073593.1","NP_001387587.1","NP_001387588.1","NP_001387589.1","NP_001387590.1","NP_001387591.1","NP_001387592.1","NP_203520.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,183],[184,199,281]],"edits":[{"start":184,"end":198,"original":"ERSSSLEGSPDEFSN","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":15,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[0,15,0],[3,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q14790-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q14790-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":8